Here's a complete implementation using ASP.NET Core's built-in middleware:

**1. Register Problem Details services and exception handler in `Program.cs`:**

```csharp
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// Add Problem Details support
builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();

var app = builder.Build();

// Global exception handler — runs for all unhandled exceptions
app.UseExceptionHandler(exceptionApp =>
{
    exceptionApp.Run(async context =>
    {
        var exception = context.Features.Get<IExceptionHandlerFeature>()?.Error;
        var (statusCode, title) = exception switch
        {
            KeyNotFoundException   => (StatusCodes.Status404NotFound,    "Not Found"),
            ArgumentException      => (StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest,  "Bad Request"),
            InvalidOperationException => (StatusCodes.Status409Conflict, "Conflict"),
            _ => (StatusCodes.Status500InternalServerError, "An error occurred")
        };

        context.Response.StatusCode = statusCode;

        var details = new ProblemDetails
        {
            Status = statusCode,
            Title  = title,
            // Only surface the message for known/expected exceptions
            Detail = exception is not null && statusCode != 500
                ? exception.Message
                : "An unexpected error occurred.",
            Instance = context.Request.Path
        };

        await context.Response.WriteAsJsonAsync(details);
    });
});

// Also convert non-exception error status codes (e.g. 404 from routing) to Problem Details
app.UseStatusCodePages();

// ... map your endpoints here ...

app.Run();
```

**2. Add the required `using` at the top if not already present:**

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Diagnostics;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;
```

**How it works:**

| Layer | What it catches |
|---|---|
| `UseExceptionHandler` | Any unhandled exception from endpoints/middleware |
| `UseStatusCodePages` | Empty error responses (e.g., 404 when no route matches) |
| `AddProblemDetails()` | Wires up the `application/problem+json` content type |

Endpoints stay clean — just throw:

```csharp
app.MapGet("/items/{id}", (int id) =>
{
    if (id < 0) throw new ArgumentException("ID must be positive");
    throw new KeyNotFoundException($"Item {id} not found");
});
```

Response:

```json
{
  "status": 404,
  "title": "Not Found",
  "detail": "Item 42 not found",
  "instance": "/items/42"
}
```

500 errors intentionally hide `detail` to avoid leaking stack traces or internal state.
